      "html" : "<\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163978\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163978\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">The surface grade of all soil absorption systems shall be located at a point lower than the surface grade of any water well or reservoir on the same or adjoining lot. Where this is not possible, the site shall be located so surface water drainage from the site is not directed toward a well or reservoir. The soil absorption system shall be located with a minimum horizontal distance between various elements as indicated in <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\"><Link class=\"Jump\" to=\"{{ pathname: '\/codes\/newyorkcity\/latest\/NYCadmin\/0-0-0-163977', hash: '#JD_PCTable1402.3' }}\">Table 1402.3<\/Link><\/span><span style=\"color: #000000;font-weight: normal;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,serif;font-size:10pt;\">. Private sewage disposal systems in compacted areas, such as parking lots and driveways, are prohibited. Surface water shall be diverted away from any soil absorption site on the same or neighboring lots.<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163979\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163979\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div><a name=\"JD_PCTable1402.3\" id=\"JD_PCTable1402.3\" title=\"PC Table 1402.3\"><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: bold;font-style: normal;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">Table 1402.3<br><\/br>Location of Subsurface Irrigation System<\/span><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-163980\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-163980\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div>",
      "id" : "12812-html-1",
      "kind" : "html",
      "plainText" : "The surface grade of all soil absorption systems shall be located at a point lower than the surface grade of any water well or reservoir on the same or adjoining lot. Where this is not possible, the site shall be located so surface water drainage from the site is not directed toward a well or reservoir. The soil absorption system shall be located with a minimum horizontal distance between various elements as indicated in Table 1402.3 . Private sewage disposal systems in compacted areas, such as parking lots and driveways, are prohibited. Surface water shall be diverted away from any soil absorption site on the same or neighboring lots. \n\n Table 1402.3\n Location of Subsurface Irrigation System"
    },
